      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/panaque-cf-titan-shampupa-l418-2/",
      "html": "<p>The magnificent panaques of the nigrolineatus complex have long been sought-after aquarium fish. All species seem to grow around 40 cm long. One of the most spectacular species comes from Peru and was given the L-number 418. It is probably identical with the described species Panaque titan, but since this is not completely certain, the animal is better called P. cf. titan in the hobby. Characteristic for the fish, which exporters call \"shampupa\" after the river in Peru where they catch the animals, are the broad, light-coloured tail fin seam and the blue-green base colouring.</p><p>Shampupa is a very rare species that is always available only in very small quantities.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/panaque-cf-titan-shampupa-l418-2/",
      "html": "<p>Like all panaques they are specialized wood eaters, so plenty of dead wood is a must for the basic equipment of a panaque aquarium. However, numerous other types of food are also accepted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/panaque-cf-titan-shampupa-l418-2/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Panaque: after the native name of P. nigrolineatus in Venezuela.</p><p>Suggestion of a common name: Shampupa Royal Pleco.</p>"
    }
  ],
